Subject: Handle supplementary Unicode case equivalents in V8
Upstream-Status: Backport [V8 f607706154eabc4a949628a88b38dbe95cd2274c]
Reference: https://github.com/v8/v8/commit/f607706154eabc4a949628a88b38dbe95cd2274c

Adapt the upstream repair to Node 26's older RegExpCaseFolding API. Preserve
UTF-16 code-unit matching in legacy mode and desugar Unicode-mode BMP
literals whose case equivalents include supplementary code points.

diff --git a/deps/v8/src/regexp/gen-regexp-special-case.cc b/deps/v8/src/regexp/gen-regexp-special-case.cc
--- a/deps/v8/src/regexp/gen-regexp-special-case.cc
+++ b/deps/v8/src/regexp/gen-regexp-special-case.cc
@@ -17,6 +17,16 @@
 static const base::uc32 kSurrogateEnd = 0xdfff;
 static const base::uc32 kNonBmpStart = 0x10000;
 
+// Backport V8 f607706154eabc4a949628a88b38dbe95cd2274c. Unicode 18 adds
+// case classes spanning BMP and supplementary code points. Legacy matching
+// compares UTF-16 code units, so Canonicalize must see BMP values only.
+bool RemoveSupplementary(icu::UnicodeSet& set) {
+  constexpr UChar32 first = static_cast<UChar32>(kNonBmpStart);
+  if (!set.containsSome(first, UCHAR_MAX_VALUE)) return false;
+  set.remove(first, UCHAR_MAX_VALUE);
+  return true;
+}
